  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Bingo (Dominoes). 28 tiles (double-6). 2 players. Trick-taking. Blanks are trump; double-blank (Bingo) is highest. Tile point values: doubles worth pip total, others 0 or pip of non-blank end. Win 70+ points in tricks, then claim. Game points: 1/2/3 based on loser's score. Match to 7 game points.",
    Player: "1. **Start**: The first tile played determines the trump suit (Blanks). 2. **Tricks**: Players play one tile each. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 3. **The Draw**: While the stock exists, players draw one tile after each trick. 4. **Trump**: The double-blank (Bingo) is the highest trump, followed by other tiles with blanks. 5. **Closing**: A player may 'close the stock' to stop drawing and force strict suit-following.",
    objective: 'Win tricks worth at least 70 points to win the deal and accumulate 7 game points to win the match.',
    gameplay: "1. **Start**: The first tile played determines the trump suit (Blanks). 2. **Tricks**: Players play one tile each. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 3. **The Draw**: While the stock exists, players draw one tile after each trick. 4. **Trump**: The double-blank (Bingo) is the highest trump, followed by other tiles with blanks. 5. **Closing**: A player may 'close the stock' to stop drawing and force strict suit-following.",
    keyRules: [
      'The double-blank (Bingo) tile beats all other tiles.',
      'Any tile with a blank end counts as a trump.',
      'Suit-following is only mandatory after the stock is closed or empty.',
      'You must actively claim victory once you reach 70 points.',
    ],
